# ONE-OFF PATCH SCRIPTS, WHICH MUST NEVER REACH A COMMIT.
#
# Edits to this repo are often applied by writing a throwaway `_name.py` that
# rewrites a source file and is then discarded. Five of them were committed and
# pushed on 2026-08-25 because the cleanup step was a `mv` into _to_delete/ and
# the bridge cannot unlink, so every one of those moves failed silently while
# the run reported success. Ignoring the pattern is the fix that does not
# depend on remembering.
_*.py

# Scratch JSON from those same throwaway scripts — snapshots, diffs, probes.
_*.json

# scratch: files the Cowork bridge cannot delete without a permission grant
_to_delete/

# BALLOTPEDIA PERSONAL EXPORT. 9.3 MB, filename says "for_kevin_deluca", and it
# arrived as a one-off export to a named person rather than an open download.
# Standing rule for that class of input: usable in class and in the analysis,
# not republished. The repo is public, so the rule has to live here and not in
# anyone's memory of it.
#
# It is also NOT load-bearing for anything committed: the feasibility check it
# was fetched for is finished and its result (92% of organisations are pure
# partisans, so the identification problem is not fixable with this data) is
# recorded in endorse_quality/PREREGISTRATION.md.
forecast/endorse_quality/ballotpedia/

# Python bytecode from running the endorse_quality scripts in place.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
